# JMX and OpenMBean Rules

## Role

JMX is an operational transport adapter.

It does not own:

- tracing domain policy
- sampling/scrubbing validation
- runtime state
- mutation authorization policy
- application-facing API
- exporter or processor lifecycle

JMX converts OpenMBean/JDK-safe values into approved API/core contracts and maps results back.

## ObjectName and Management Contract

ObjectNames, attribute names, operation names, and Open Types are external operational contracts.

Define them centrally.

Avoid names derived from implementation class names.

Do not register duplicate or unstable names.

Because the solution is pre-production, justified clean replacement is allowed, but update all:

- tests
- docs
- dashboards/scripts
- deployment guidance
- warning registers

Do not keep dual old/new MBeans by default.

## Open Types

Use JMX Open Types or bounded JDK-safe values:

- `String`
- primitive wrappers
- arrays where bounded
- `CompositeData`
- `TabularData`
- explicit maps converted at the boundary

Do not expose:

- implementation objects
- Spring beans
- OTel SDK objects
- mutable collections
- arbitrary serializable classes
- class names for reconstruction

Do not use Java native serialization.

Use string wire values instead of Java enum instances across classloader boundaries.

## Transport Conversion

Keep conversion isolated:

```text
OpenMBean/JMX input
    -> bounded transport conversion
    -> control-protocol decode
    -> domain validation
    -> mutation policy
    -> apply/read
    -> OpenMBean/JMX result
```

Do not apply raw maps directly to runtime state.

Do not duplicate domain validation in the MBean implementation.

Conversion failures must return bounded, machine-readable diagnostics without exposing raw payloads.

## Registration Lifecycle

Registration must be:

- explicitly owned
- idempotent
- safe when an ObjectName already exists
- reversible
- rollback-safe after partial registration
- classloader-safe
- cleaned up on shutdown

Do not register MBeans in static initializers.

Do not retain application classloaders through platform/agent global registries.

Define ownership when both application and agent planes can register management endpoints.

## Read and Mutation Operations

Read operations are side-effect-free.

Mutation operations:

- are disabled by default
- use the approved runtime-control gate
- validate before apply
- preserve LKG on rejection/failure
- return applied/current version and status
- do not expose mutable state

An MBean cannot bypass core mutation policy.

## Readiness

MBean presence is not equivalent to extension or telemetry-pipeline readiness.

Readiness should use the approved versioned descriptor and capability model.

Do not infer sampler, processor, sanitizer, propagation, or exporter readiness from one registration marker.

## Security

JMX is a privileged administrative surface.

Code-level validation does not replace:

- JVM JMX configuration
- authentication
- authorization
- TLS
- network policy
- Kubernetes RBAC
- host/container security

Do not expose public unauthenticated remote JMX.

Do not log:

- credentials
- raw mutation payloads
- PII
- full environment
- sensitive patterns
- implementation dumps

Tracing identifiers are not authorization proof.

## Diagnostics

Expose bounded operational facts such as:

- mode
- readiness lifecycle
- capabilities
- mutation gate
- applied policy version
- state fingerprint
- last rejection code
- bounded warning summary

Do not expose raw policy content when it may contain sensitive keys or patterns.

## Testing

Unit/integration tests should cover:

- ObjectName stability
- Open Type schema
- conversion
- invalid shape/type
- unsupported protocol version
- read without mutation
- mutation disabled
- successful apply
- rejection preserves state
- duplicate registration
- partial registration rollback
- unregister/shutdown

Run real E2E for:

- application/agent classloader separation
- JMX wire round trip
- readiness descriptor
- agent-only and application modes
- version mismatch
- runtime mutation

A skipped required JMX E2E is `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`.
